+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional due dates, consistent overdue status, and API/UI overdue filters for ticket `adw/demo-todo#1`.
+
+**Architecture:** Extend the existing records and singleton store with `DateOnly?` and shared overdue filtering. Track whether PATCH supplied `dueDate`, independently of its nullable value. Blazor continues to call the store directly.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit/WebApplicationFactory, Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-todo-due-date-design.md` (approved).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Keine neuen NuGet-Pakete, keine Persistenz, Erinnerungen oder neue Sortierung.
+- `dueDate` is an optional `YYYY-MM-DD` calendar date; no time component.
+- Overdue means unfinished and strictly before the current UTC date.
+- PATCH omission preserves the date; explicit `null` removes it.
+- Invalid requests return HTTP 400 with `{"error":"..."}` and change no data.
+- UI controls used by tests have `data-testid`; screenshots stay outside the repository.
+- Work on `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos` in the existing checkout; draft PR targets `main`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Legacy payloads without dates still work, including title-only and done-only PATCH (Task 1).
+- Leap days and impossible dates use real calendar validation, not a shape-only check (Task 1).
+- Rejected PATCH combining a valid title with an invalid date is atomic (Task 1).
+- Completing an overdue todo removes it from the filter; clearing its date does too (Task 2).
+- Keyboard toggling and a filter with no matches preserve a usable list (Task 3).
+
+---
+
